<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turmātim</span></b> , adv.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>by troops</i> or <i>squadrons</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equites se turmatim explicare coeperunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 93</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nostri turmatim in eum devenerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vagantibus circa moenia turmatim barbaris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					5, 39, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 28, 13, 9 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>in
			troops</i>, <i>in bands</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpora turmatim certantia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 118</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>